  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "As your Command phase begins, you may choose one combat doctrine from the three below. Until your next Command phase starts, it applies to every friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit that has this ability. Assault Doctrine: an advance move leaves the unit still able to declare a charge later that turn. Devastator Doctrine: [ASSAULT] applies to the unit's ranged attacks. Tactical Doctrine: a fall-back move leaves the unit still able to shoot and to declare a charge later that turn. Unless a rule says otherwise, your army may choose each combat doctrine only once per battle, and a unit can have just one combat doctrine active; if some rule activates a new one for that unit, the earlier one stops applying to it.",
